READ THIS BEFORE ACTING ON THE TABLE ABOVE
  - Buckets differing by a few hundredths of R on a few hundred trades is not a
    regime effect. The panel's own trade floor is 200 per fold, and its names are
    correlated at rho 0.24-0.47, so a bucket's N is worth well under its face value.
  - Breadth is computed on TODAY's index membership. It reads HIGH exactly where the
    real index was shedding names, and there is no matched control to cancel that
    here the way there is for a strategy's avgR.
  - A gradient that appears in FIT and not in SELECT is the same result the 13
    rejected confluence filters produced. Only a bucket ordering that holds in FIT,
    SELECT and all three TEST folds is worth turning into a gate.
